    {
      "id": "SFPL",
      "code_hash": "e8ad7ac6710046b860c353d0fc47d1c5",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"what-can-be-maintained\">What can be maintained</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A view that is quietly wrong is worse than no view, so the rule is\nstrict. Filters, computed columns, inner joins (self-joins too), cross\njoins, <code>UNION ALL</code> and <code>ORDER BY</code> are maintained from their changes.\nEverything else is <strong>recomputed and diffed</strong> on every refresh instead\nof being maintained wrongly: left, semi and anti joins (a left join's\nNULL-padded rows must be <em>retracted</em> when a match turns up later),\n<code>DISTINCT</code>, <code>LIMIT</code> (it depends on row order), windows, and aggregates\n(contracts work on them, but their update rules aren't proved yet).\nThe result is just as right, but it costs a full run per refresh, and\n<code>node.status()</code> tells you which kind of node you have. Pick one:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
